        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.85,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "which we can call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 141.31,
          "en": "And as the name suggests, this is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.31,
          "end": 143.233,
          "en": "that helps us write to a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.57,
          "end": 147.07999999999998,
          "en": "There always is the writeTextFile method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.07999999999998,
          "end": 150.21,
          "en": "which makes writings on text to a file even easier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.21,
          "end": 152.81,
          "en": "but to see more Deno features in action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.81,
          "end": 154.333,
          "en": "I'm going to go for writeFile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.71,
          "end": 160.12,
          "en": "Now, writeFile wants two main arguments here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.12,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "it wants a path to the file, including the file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 167.14,
          "en": "and the data that should be written to the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.14,
          "end": 170.3,
          "en": "And the data should be a Uint8Array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.3,
          "end": 173.05,
          "en": "which is a strange data type, but which is actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.05,
          "end": 176.89,
          "en": "a core data type built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.89,
          "end": 180.81,
          "en": "which in the end is an array full of bytes, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "Now, we will be able to convert our text to bytes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 187.14,
          "en": "So it's no problem that we have no bytes right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.14,
          "end": 188.61,
          "en": "but that we only have a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.61,
          "end": 191.47,
          "en": "Let's start with the first argument, the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.47,
          "end": 193.21,
          "en": "And here let's say we wanna create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.21,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "that file in the same folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 197.66,
          "en": "Conveniently, the only thing we then need to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.66,
          "end": 199.92000000000002,
          "en": "is specify a file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.92000000000002,
          "end": 203.443,
          "en": "So here I'm going to create my message.TXT file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.35,
          "end": 208.25,
          "en": "The second argument should be the data that we wanna store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.25,
          "end": 211.16,
          "en": "and that should be this byte array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.16,
          "end": 215.5,
          "en": "Now, actually here this preview snippet gives me an idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.5,
          "end": 220.5,
          "en": "on how we can convert the string to such a bytes array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.18,
          "end": 226.18,
          "en": "We simply create an encoder by instantiating a new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.7,
          "end": 231.7,
          "en": "text encoder that is a globally available feature in Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "If we go to the Deno docs and we search for text encoder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 240.573,
          "en": "we see that is a globally available constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.54,
          "end": 243.68,
          "en": "And in the end, this creates an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.68,
          "end": 247.28,
          "en": "that helps us convert text to bytes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.28,
          "end": 251.73,
          "en": "So our data then is encoder.encode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.73,
          "end": 255.22,
          "en": "and to encode we pass our text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.22,
          "end": 257.9,
          "en": "And then it's the data, the encoded text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.9,
          "end": 261.173,
          "en": "which we feed as a second argument to writeFile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.592,
          "end": 265.85,
          "en": "No, that's not too fancy, but that's our first Deno code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.85,
          "end": 266.713,
          "en": "we can write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.74,
          "end": 270.97,
          "en": "Now, Deno, as I mentioned on a slide earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.97,
          "end": 275.7,
          "en": "embraces modern JavaScript features like Promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.7,
          "end": 278.84000000000003,
          "en": "Therefore writeFile does not take a call back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 278.84000000000003,
          "end": 280.95,
          "en": "to let us know once it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.95,
          "end": 284.17,
          "en": "Instead here, we now can call then or a catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.17,
          "end": 287.123,
          "en": "because writeFile returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.12,
          "end": 292.49,
          "en": "So here with then we can listen for the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.8,
          "end": 296.63,
          "en": "success of this write operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.63,
          "end": 298.53,
          "en": "and we can then do whatever we want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.53,
          "end": 302.67,
          "en": "For example, we can console.log \"wrote to file\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.67,
          "end": 304.72,
          "en": "and be done with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.72,
          "end": 307.94,
          "en": "Now, if we execute this file, if we save it and run it with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.94,
          "end": 312.94,
          "en": "Deno Run, we should have a script that writes to a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.28,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "But actually what happens is that we get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "a permission denied error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 322.75,
          "en": "Well, and that is actually a key feature of Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.75,
          "end": 324.553,
          "en": "So what's up with this error?",
          "zh": ""
        }
